{
  "id": "navigation/declaration/07_changed_signatures",
  "topic": "navigation",
  "subtopic": "declaration",
  "title": "A definition whose declaration changed",
  "summary": "Go-to-declaration on a definition that no longer matches its declaration reaches the declaration it parted from",
  "prose": "When a parameter changes on one side only, the definition and the header\ndeclaration become two functions, and the definition has no declaration of\nits own. Go-to-declaration on it falls back to the functions of its name and\nlinkage in its scope that nothing defines: the declaration that wants the\nsame edit, a `static` one's in its own file. An overload with a definition\nof its own is no candidate, nor is a function of another linkage or of an\nanonymous namespace it is not in. A method defined in its class never had a\ndeclaration apart, and a template or a system header's function is left\nalone: those are declared where they are defined.",
  "status": "supported",
